the training state carries a momentum buffer for every parameter beyond the parameters: true
the interrupted run stops mid-epoch: true
the interrupted run's losses are the uninterrupted run's first ones: true
the fresh process restores the step, epoch, data position and batch order: true
the resumed run's final parameters equal the uninterrupted run's, bit for bit: true
the resumed run's per-step losses equal the uninterrupted run's, bit for bit: true
the restored host generator draws what the saved one would have: true
a resume restoring the parameters but not the momentum ends elsewhere: true
a resume restarting the host generator ends elsewhere: true
restoring a state set without the momentum is refused, naming the difference: true
a plain Persistence checkpoint is refused as recording no progress: true
the checkpoint records the one random seed it was saved under: true
a resume under a different random seed is refused, naming both seeds: true
a checkpoint of a graph built under a scoped seed restores under that scoped seed: true
a resume whose graph was built under another scoped seed is refused, naming both: true
a checkpoint recording one seed twice restores under that seed: true
a format-1 checkpoint, recording no seed, restores under another seed with a warning: true
a format-2 checkpoint missing its seed is refused as malformed: true
an appending save replaces the metadata key it names and keeps the others: true
the mixed-precision run backs the scale off after the stop step: true
the mixed-precision run skips an outlier step after the stop step: true
the mixed-precision run takes an optimizer step after the stop step: true
the mixed-precision run's losses are finite: true
the mixed-precision loss is an f16 activation: true
the mixed-precision masters stay single: true
the resumed mixed-precision run's losses, z-scores, skips and scales equal the uninterrupted run's, bit for bit: true
the resumed mixed-precision run's final master weights equal the uninterrupted run's, bit for bit: true
a resume re-creating the loss scaler ends on other master weights: true
a resume re-creating the outlier detector ends on other master weights: true
restoring the scaler's state into one with another growth interval is refused, naming both: true
restoring the detector's state into one over another window is refused, naming both: true
